<title>GERMANY: ATHLETICS-JACKSON CLOCKS SEASON BEST.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-JACKSON CLOCKS SEASON BEST.</headline>
<dateline>INGOLSTADT, Germany 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>World record holder Colin Jackson recorded his best time of the season in the 110 metres hurdles at a meeting in Ingolstadt on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Briton, who set a world record 12.91 in Stuttgart in 1993, won the race in 13.24 seconds ahead of Germany's Falk Balzer (13.46).</p>
<p>Olympic bronze medallist Florian Schwarthoff was expected to provide a stiff challenge to Jackson but the German withdrew shortly before the race in this southern German town, citing a slight injury he sustained at last Wednesday's grand prix meeting in Nice.</p>
</text>
